'''RJ-83''', or simply referred as '''RJ''', was the personal [[droid]] of [[Nash Durango]]<ref name="Meet the Young Jedi" /> and also a friend to the [[Jedi Initiate]]s [[Kai Brightstar]], [[Lys Solay]], and [[Nubs]] during the [[High Republic Era]].<ref name="YJA" />

==Biography==
RJ-83 was an [[RJ unit]] who was active as the [[Pilot|copilot]] of [[Nash Durango]]. With their [[shuttle]], the [[Crimson Firehawk]], they worked for [[Durango Shuttle Service]], a company owned by Durango's [[Durangos|parents]]. In [[232 BBY]], they were sent to [[Coruscant]] in one of the shuttles delivering [[Jedi Initiate|Jedi younglings]] to the [[Tenoo Jedi Temple|Jedi Temple]] on their [[homeworld]] [[Tenoo]]. They transported the three younglings [[Kai Brightstar]], [[Lys Solay]] and [[Nubs]]. When they arrived on Tenoo, they were contacted by [[Hap]], a [[chef]] who operated [[Hap's Sap Tap]] in [[Kublop Springs]]. He asked them for help, as his [[Cafe|café]] was being [[Raid on Hap's Sap Tap|raided]] by a [[Taborr's gang|gang]] of [[pirate]]s led by [[Cyrus Vuundir|Taborr Val Dorn]]. When they arrived in Kublop Springs, RJ-83 and Durango stayed with the ship. After a short fight, the pirates attempted to escape with their loot. The Jedi contacted Durango, who arrived with the Firehawk. With RJ-83's help, she used a crane hook to pull up the cart with Hap's stolen belongings. This distracted the pirates long enough for the Jedi and several local residents to arrive, forcing the pirates to leave empty-handed. RJ-83 and Durango later transported the Jedi to the temple.<ref name="The Young Jedi" />

As the [[Crimson Firehawk]] flew through an [[Asteroid field]], RJ-83 and Durango noticed an alarm begin to blare due to an asteroid hitting the ship. RJ went outside the ship to repair, but lost a tool as it tripped over a metal protrusion. RJ jumped after it before he went back, hopping asteroid to asteroid. RJ finished repairing the ship before it headed back inside to Durango.<ref name="RJ Repairs the Firehawk">{{FunWithNubs|RJ Repairs the Firehawk}}</ref>

{{Droid-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
RJ-83 first appeared in the short "[[Meet the Young Jedi]]" of the [[Disney Junior]] animated series ''[[Star Wars: Young Jedi Adventures]]''.<ref name="Meet the Young Jedi" /> RJ-83 was voiced by [[Jonathan Lipow]].<ref name="YJA" />

